 "chunks": [
  {
   "text": "On November twentieth, 2026,",
   "start": 0.7,
   "end": 3.125
  },
  {
   "text": "the mathematician Levent Alpöge posted a four-page note.",
   "start": 3.125,
   "end": 6.862
  },
  {
   "text": "He wrote that he believes that, working with Claude,",
   "start": 6.862,
   "end": 9.575
  },
  {
   "text": "he has found a proof of the Riemann Hypothesis,",
   "start": 9.575,
   "end": 12.3
  },
  {
   "text": "perhaps the most famous open problem in mathematics.",
   "start": 12.3,
   "end": 15.862
  },
  {
   "text": "Instead of a written proof, he posted 17 million lines of Lean,",
   "start": 15.862,
   "end": 20.188
  },
  {
   "text": "a language in which a computer checks every step.",
   "start": 20.188,
   "end": 23.087
  },
  {
   "text": "A day later, the communities behind Lean and its shared math library,",
   "start": 23.55,
   "end": 27.738
  },
  {
   "text": "Mathlib, wrote, quote: we have full confidence that Alpöge's proof of the Riemann",
   "start": 27.738,
   "end": 32.8
  },
  {
   "text": "Hypothesis is correct.",
   "start": 32.8,
   "end": 34.675
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's the road from the primes to that claim.",
   "start": 35.6,
   "end": 38.15
  }
 ],
